ite constitutional symptoms, the presence of blasts and pancytopenia (anemia + thrombocytopenia) makes hematologic malignancy more likely than infection", "Metabolic or Endocrine Crisis: Normal serum electrolytes and glucose reduce suspicion for acute metabolic derangement, though diabetes remains a comorbidity to monitor"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Significant leukocytosis with blasts", "Anemia and thrombocytopenia"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.005, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Neurologic findings (ataxia, visual decline) are atypical for acute myeloid leukemia (B1) and may suggest alternative diagnoses, but they do not strongly favor…"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3514257739451718, "posterior": 0.39495914218367945, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss) are common in lymphoid neoplasms but less specific. The LR+ of 6.0 for B2 suggests moderate increase in likelihood…"], "evidence_against": ["The absence of lymphoid-specific features (e.g., skin lesions, endocrine abnormalities) weakly argues against lymphoid neoplasm (B2), though constitutional sym…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4337359667279197, "posterior": 0.487465