ite constitutional symptoms, the presence of blasts and pancytopenia (anemia + thrombocytopenia) makes hematologic malignancy more likely than infection", "Metabolic or Endocrine Crisis: Normal serum electrolytes and glucose reduce suspicion for acute metabolic derangement, though diabetes remains a comorbidity to monitor"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Significant leukocytosis with blasts", "Anemia and thrombocytopenia"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.004529511328404318, "posterior": 0.0001813349742405251, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Pancytopenia is consistent with blast crisis in B3 despite a weak exclusion by anemia alone. The LR reference for anemia weakly reduces B3's likelihood, but bl…"], "evidence_against": ["Neurologic findings (ataxia, visual decline) are atypical for acute myeloid leukemia (B1) and may suggest alternative diagnoses, but they do not strongly favor…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.39495914218367945, "posterior": 0.527749249848596, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Constitutional symptoms with LR+ 6.0 moderately support lymphoid neoplasm (B2). However, the presence of 35% blasts (pathognomonic for myeloid processes) creat…"], "evidence_against": ["Absence of lymphoid-specific features weakly argues against B2, but constitutional symptoms remain moderate evidence for lymphoid neoplasm. This creates a slig…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4874656273213329, "posterior": 0.3886255960490536, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Blast crisis in chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm (B3) explains both the subacute course and high blast count. Constitutional symptoms are nonspecific here, …"], "evidence_against": ["Pancytopenia is consistent with blast crisis in B3 despite a weak exclusion by anemia alone. The LR reference for anemia weakly reduces B3's likelihood, but bl…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.082, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["35% blasts in peripheral blood are pathognomonic for myeloid neoplasm (B1), which includes acute myeloid leukemia and myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blas…"]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.001, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["35% blasts are pathognomonic for malignancy, making reactive leukocytosis (B5) unlikely. Anemia and thrombocytopenia are consistent with myeloid processes (B1)…"]}}, "frontier": ["B2", "B3", "B1"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the finding of pancytopenia (anemia + thrombocytopenia) inconsistent with chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm in accelerated phase (B3)?", "summary": "Pancytopenia is common in advanced myeloproliferative neoplasms like blast crisis (B3), so this finding is consistent with B3 rather than disconfirming it. However, the LR Reference for B3 under 'Anemia' shows weak exclusion."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss) with an LR+ of 6.0 for lymphoid neoplasm (B2) provide stronger support for B2 despite the 35% blasts typically favoring myeloid proce…", "summary": "Constitutional symptoms with LR+ 6.0 moderately support lymphoid neoplasm (B2). However, the presence of 35% blasts (pathognomonic for myeloid processes) creates a minor conflict, slightly favoring B1 over B2."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute course with blast crisis in chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm (B3) explain the constitutional symptoms and 35% blasts in peripheral blood?", "summary": "Blast crisis in chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm (B3) explains both the subacute course and high blast count. Constitutional symptoms are nonspecific here, providing minimal incremental support."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Could the mild anemia and thrombocytopenia be due to non-malignant causes, supporting reactive leukocytosis (B5) despite the presence of 35% blasts in peripheral blood?", "summary": "35% blasts are pathognomonic for malignancy, making reactive leukocytosis (B5) unlikely. Anemia and thrombocytopenia are consistent with myeloid processes (B1) or blast crisis (B3), not non-malignant causes."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the absent lymphoid-specific features (e.g., skin lesions, endocrine abnormalities) inconsistent with the diagnosis of lymphoid neoplasm (B2) despite constitutional symptoms?", "summary": "Absence of lymphoid-specific features weakly argues against B2, but constitutional symptoms remain moderate evidence for lymphoid neoplasm. This creates a slight reduction in B2's likelihood."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the presence of pancytopenia (anemia + thrombocytopenia) inconsistent with chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm (B3) given the LR reference for anemia weakly excludes it?", "summary": "Pancytopenia is consistent with blast crisis in B3 despite a weak exclusion by anemia alone. The LR reference for anemia weakly reduces B3's likelihood, but blast count maintains its plausibility."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B3", 0.434], ["B2", 0.351], ["B4", 0.131]]}, {"top": [["B3", 0.487], ["B2", 0.395], ["B4", 0.103]]}, {"top": [["B2", 0.528], ["B3", 0.389], ["B4", 0.082]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "Patient is hemodynamically stable with no airway compromise, severe respiratory compromise, or shock. Neurological findings (ataxia, visual decline) are atypical but not immediately life-threatening. Constitutional symptoms and lab abnormalities suggest a hematologic malignancy requiring further investigation, not urgent intervention.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading branch B2 (lymphoid neoplasm) has posterior 0.528 < 0.75 threshold. Dangerous alternative B2 (posterior 0.528, danger 0.8) remains unresolved. Required discriminators (blast morphology, flow cytometry) are still available to differentiate myeloid vs lymphoid neoplasms."}, "turn_budget_used": 3, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.8, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.527749249848596, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'elevated red blood cell count', 'Macrothrombocytopenia', 'Leukocytosis', 'Myeloproliferative disorder', 'elevated white blood cell count'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "program_faults": [], "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B3", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.434}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "posterior": 0.528, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 1}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 3, "disconfirming": 5, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Absence of lymphoid-specific features weakly argues against B2, but constitutional symptoms remain moderate evidence fo…"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B3", "B4"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=75%, source=primekg]\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis,